{number: 74}
{title: I Must Tell Jesus}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] I must tell Jesus all of my trials;
I cannot bear these [G7] burdens a-[C] lone;
In my distress He kindly will help me;
He ever [G7] loves and cares for His [C] own.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
I must tell [F] Jesus! I must tell [C] Jesus!
I cannot bear my [G7] burdens a-[C] lone;
I must tell [F] Jesus! I must tell [C] Jesus!
Jesus can [G7] help me, Jesus a-[C] lone.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] I must tell Jesus all of my troubles;
He is a kind, com-[G7] passionate [C] Friend;
If I but ask Him, He will deliver,
Make of my [G7] troubles quickly an [C] end.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Tempted and tried, I need a great Savior,
One who can help my [G7] burdens to [C] bear;
I must tell Jesus, I must tell Jesus;
He all my [G7] cares and sorrows will [C] share.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
O [C] how the world to evil allures me!
O how my heart is [G7] tempted to [C] sin!
I must tell Jesus, and He will help me
Over the [G7] world the victory to [C] win.
{end_of_verse}
